#!/command/with-contenv bash
# One database dump a day into /config/backups, fourteen kept: the script
# every way of installing runs (containers/dump/dump-daily), here as the
# programs' user through the database's local socket. A copy on the same
# disk guards against a bad update or a mistake, not a dead disk: copy
# the config folder somewhere else as well.
set -euo pipefail
. /opt/hikari/aio/env

program \
    PATH="$PGBIN:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin" \
    PGHOST=/run/postgresql PGUSER=hikari PGDATABASE=hikari \
    /opt/hikari/dump-daily /config/backups
